sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant PG as PostgreSQL
  participant RelayA as Relay A
  participant RelayB as Relay B
  participant Queue as BullMQ on Valkey
  participant WorkerA as Worker process A
  participant Systemd as systemd
  participant WorkerB as Worker process B
  participant Handler as Durable handler

  PG->>RelayA: Claim unpublished event with lease token
  RelayA->>Queue: Add deterministic jobId
  Queue-->>RelayA: Job accepted
  Note over RelayA,PG: Crash window: relay dies before outbox acknowledgement
  RelayA--xPG: No acknowledgement
  PG->>PG: Lease expires and event becomes claimable
  PG->>RelayB: Claim the same event with a new lease token
  RelayB->>Queue: Add the same deterministic jobId
  Queue-->>RelayB: Converge on one retained job
  RelayB->>PG: Acknowledge with the current lease token

  Queue->>WorkerA: Deliver eventId and handlerVersion
  WorkerA->>Handler: Look up persisted job result
  Handler->>PG: SELECT result by eventId and handlerVersion
  Systemd-xWorkerA: SIGKILL main process
  Queue->>Queue: Active lock expires or the job is retried
  Systemd->>WorkerB: Restart service with a different process ID
  Queue->>WorkerB: Deliver the same logical job again
  WorkerB->>Handler: Handle duplicate delivery
  Handler->>PG: Look up persisted job result

  alt Result was committed before the kill
    PG-->>Handler: Existing succeeded or terminal result
    Handler-->>WorkerB: Return it without repeating the side effect
  else No result was committed before the kill
    PG-->>Handler: No result
    Handler->>Handler: Retry under the handler's duplicate-safety contract
    Handler->>PG: INSERT result with unique eventId and handlerVersion
    PG-->>Handler: One canonical result wins
  end

  WorkerB-->>Systemd: Active after restart
  Systemd->>PG: Verify result-key uniqueness
  Note over Systemd,PG: This proves at-least-once convergence, not exactly-once external side effects
  Note over PG,Handler: The separate PostgreSQL-polled verification email path does not use BullMQ.<br/>A provider accepted-before-ack retry may resend the same expiring single-use token<br/>with the same non-secret correlation tag
